PRE-EXISTING / ENVIRONMENT BUILD BLOCKERS (no red-as-green — full disclosure)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The whole-app macOS + iOS build of THIS repository state does NOT compile. Every error is
in PRE-EXISTING files unrelated to this page; ZERO diagnostics were ever attributed to any
of the 8 new TeslaChargingHistory*.swift files across 6 full build attempts. The blockers,
in the order they surface:

  B1. Duplicate source filename `ScheduledExportsPanel.swift` in two compiled roots
      (`TeslaSync/feature-views/` defines ScheduledExportsPanelView; `TeslaSync/Features/System/`
      defines ScheduledExportsPanel). Swift requires unique basenames per module
      -> "error: filename used twice". Both are in HEAD; neither touched by this page.
      (Verified: the only duplicate basename across all compiled roots.)

  B2. Duplicate design-token enums: `TeslaSync/Features/System/StatusApiDocsPage.swift:399`
      re-declares `enum TSSpacing { sm/md/lg/... }` (and `TSRadius`), colliding module-wide
      with the generated `apps/design/generated/apple/Tokens.swift` -> every `TSSpacing.sm`
      reference is "ambiguous use of 'sm'". Pre-existing; not referenced by this page.

  B3. Xcode-26.5-SDK `#Preview` macro regression: on this SDK `import SwiftUI` makes the
      transitively-loaded `AppKit.Preview` (macOS) / `UIKit.Preview` (iOS) macro visible, so
      `#Preview { ... }` is "ambiguous use of 'Preview'" in ~76 pre-existing files (every file
      with an `#if DEBUG #Preview`). Strippable (all such blocks are `#if DEBUG`-guarded), but
      it is an SDK-level regression, not codebase code.

  B4. Xcode-26.5-SDK `accessibilityAddTraits` / `accessibilityHint` regression: SwiftUI's own
      `View.*` and `ModifiedContent.*` overloads are reported "ambiguous" when chained on a
      ModifiedContent. 63 pre-existing files call `.accessibilityAddTraits(.updatesFrequently)`;
      they are NOT DEBUG-gated and cannot be excluded (each AI surface cluster is internally
      referenced). This is the hard, non-workaroundable blocker.

